      "id": "edHBymJeD0M",
      "title": "\"Marigold\" by Nirvana : Vocals Only",
      "publishedAt": "2023-06-17T02:06:32Z",
      "durationSec": 154,
      "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/edHBymJeD0M/mqdefault.jpg",
      "description": "\"Marigold\" was released as the B-side to the lead single of Nirvana's third album, \"In Utero\". What's interesting about it though is the fact that it's the only Nirvana song which does not feature Kurt Cobain on lead vocals, and it is also the only song to have not been written by Kurt.\n\nAs a result, there has been speculation over the years among Nirvana fans as for whether Kurt is in \"Marigold\" at all. There is an unreleased outtake version which features Kurt playing the drums, but in the official release, only Dave Grohl and Krist Novoselic are credited for the song. However, that hasn't stopped some fans from speculating that Kurt does the backing vocals in \"Marigold\".\n\nDo you believe Kurt is in \"Marigold\"? I personally don't believe he is, however I will leave it up to you to decide for yourself. ;)",
      "chapters": []
    }
